WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.466
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.766 --> 00:00:09.396
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.696 --> 00:00:16.180
Unit twenty-two: Markets of Cambodia. In this unit, you will shop at a market using too and enough.

4
00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:17.964
Market.

5
00:00:18.664 --> 00:00:22.068
Market means a place where people buy and sell things.

6
00:00:22.368 --> 00:00:24.426
Psar Thmei is a famous market.

7
00:00:25.126 --> 00:00:28.184
Your turn. Say: Market.

8
00:00:30.884 --> 00:00:31.793
Market.

9
00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:33.506
Vendor.

10
00:00:34.206 --> 00:00:36.577
Vendor means a person who sells things.

11
00:00:36.877 --> 00:00:38.876
The vendor sells fresh mangoes.

12
00:00:39.576 --> 00:00:41.567
Your turn. Say: Vendor.

13
00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:45.117
Vendor.

14
00:00:46.117 --> 00:00:46.874
Bargain.

15
00:00:47.574 --> 00:00:50.142
Bargain means to talk about the price to make it lower.

16
00:00:50.442 --> 00:00:52.198
Tourists like to bargain at the market.

17
00:00:52.898 --> 00:00:55.376
Your turn. Say: Bargain.

18
00:00:58.076 --> 00:00:58.776
Bargain.

19
00:00:59.783 --> 00:01:00.413
Cheap.

20
00:01:01.113 --> 00:01:03.008
Cheap means costing little money.

21
00:01:03.308 --> 00:01:04.901
The T-shirts are very cheap.

22
00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:07.696
Your turn. Say: Cheap.

23
00:01:10.396 --> 00:01:11.084
Cheap.

24
00:01:12.083 --> 00:01:13.201
Expensive.

25
00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:16.074
Expensive means costing a lot of money.

26
00:01:16.374 --> 00:01:18.304
This silk scarf is expensive.

27
00:01:19.004 --> 00:01:21.842
Your turn. Say: Expensive.

28
00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:25.625
Expensive.

29
00:01:26.617 --> 00:01:27.606
Souvenir.

30
00:01:28.306 --> 00:01:31.223
Souvenir means something you buy to remember a place.

31
00:01:31.523 --> 00:01:33.546
I bought a souvenir for my cousin.

32
00:01:34.246 --> 00:01:37.026
Your turn. Say: Souvenir.

33
00:01:39.726 --> 00:01:40.773
Souvenir.

34
00:01:41.783 --> 00:01:42.483
Fresh.

35
00:01:43.183 --> 00:01:45.368
Fresh means recently picked or made.

36
00:01:45.668 --> 00:01:47.284
The fish is very fresh.

37
00:01:47.984 --> 00:01:50.567
Your turn. Say: Fresh.

38
00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:54.071
Fresh.

39
00:01:55.083 --> 00:01:55.841
Busy.

40
00:01:56.541 --> 00:01:58.087
Busy means full of people.

41
00:01:58.387 --> 00:02:00.282
The market is busy on Sunday.

42
00:02:00.982 --> 00:02:03.786
Your turn. Say: Busy.

43
00:02:06.486 --> 00:02:07.359
Busy.

44
00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:10.605
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:10.905 --> 00:02:12.324
How much is this scarf?

46
00:02:13.617 --> 00:02:14.664
Twenty dollars.

47
00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:17.891
Hmm, that's too expensive for me.

48
00:02:19.183 --> 00:02:21.557
Fifteen? It's real Khmer silk.

49
00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.491
Sorry, I don't have enough money. Ten?

50
00:02:26.783 --> 00:02:28.739
OK, twelve. Deal!

51
00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:32.061
Grammar focus: Too and enough.

52
00:02:32.361 --> 00:02:35.002
It's too expensive. I don't have enough money.

53
00:02:35.302 --> 00:02:38.616
'Too' means more than you want. 'Enough' means as much as you need.

54
00:02:39.617 --> 00:02:42.420
Now read and listen. A Morning at the Market.

55
00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.567
Markets in Cambodia are busy and colourful.

56
00:02:46.883 --> 00:02:50.067
Vendors sell fresh food, clothes and souvenirs.

57
00:02:51.383 --> 00:02:54.300
At some markets, people bargain for a good price.

58
00:02:55.617 --> 00:02:58.139
Some things are cheap, and some are too expensive.

59
00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:03.133
If you don't have enough money, smile and try to bargain politely.

60
00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:07.011
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:07.311 --> 00:03:08.985
It's blank expensive for me.

62
00:03:09.285 --> 00:03:12.498
A, too. B, enough. C, very much.

63
00:03:16.483 --> 00:03:18.727
The answer is A: too.

64
00:03:20.217 --> 00:03:21.694
I don't have blank money.

65
00:03:21.994 --> 00:03:24.718
A, enough. B, too. C, many.

66
00:03:28.717 --> 00:03:30.739
The answer is A: enough.

67
00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.935
Something you buy to remember a place is a blank.

68
00:03:35.235 --> 00:03:38.319
A, souvenir. B, vendor. C, market.

69
00:03:42.317 --> 00:03:44.258
The answer is A: souvenir.

70
00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:48.623
Now it's your turn to speak. What would you buy at a market?

71
00:03:53.923 --> 00:04:00.093
I would buy fresh fruit and a krama as a souvenir. If something is too expensive, I would bargain politely.

72
00:04:00.393 --> 00:04:02.323
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:03.317 --> 00:04:06.967
Great work today! You learned eight new words and too and enough.

74
00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:10.582
Today's value is honesty. Always tell the truth.

75
00:04:10.882 --> 00:04:14.776
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

76
00:04:15.076 --> 00:04:17.903
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

